# Keep the build context lean (Dockerfile only needs requirements.txt, src/, main.py)
.git
.github
__pycache__/
**/__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
.venv/
venv/

# Frontend: skip sources/node_modules/tests, but KEEP the built SPA (frontend/dist).
# The Dockerfile copies frontend/dist so a single container can serve the UI itself
# (src/api/server.py mounts /assets and serves "/" from it) — the self-hosting story in
# SELF_HOSTING.md / docker-compose.yml. Excluding ALL of frontend/ while the Dockerfile
# still did `COPY frontend` is what broke every Render build ("/frontend: not found").
# Listed explicitly rather than as `frontend/*` + `!frontend/dist`, because exclude-then-
# re-include ordering is easy to get subtly wrong and this must not break the build again.
frontend/node_modules/
frontend/src/
frontend/public/
frontend/e2e/
frontend/tests/
frontend/coverage/
frontend/playwright-report/
frontend/test-results/
frontend/.vercel/
frontend/*.json
frontend/*.js
frontend/*.ts
frontend/*.cjs
frontend/*.mjs
frontend/*.html
frontend/*.lock
frontend/dist/**/*.map
static/
logo/

# Docs, tests, drafts, data, infra
tests/
drafts/
docs/
db/
migrations/
packages/
*.md
docker-compose*.yml
Makefile
render.yaml

# Secrets / local
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.log
logs/
chroma_db/
*.sqlite
*.db
